  "cases": [
    "Sixth Sense on an opponent creature binds source damage subject controller and optional draw",
    "recipient noncombat damage does not trigger Sixth Sense despite a current grant",
    "Combat Research draws for its recipient and ignores an unrelated same-name creature",
    "removing the grant after detection preserves the stacked trigger but prevents future triggers",
    "Custody Battle follows recipient upkeeps and transfers control after the native choice",
    "recipient renewal cannot replace the captured source of an established trigger",
    "granter renewal and reattachment cannot supply an earlier trigger declaration instance",
    "control changes affect future grants while an existing trigger keeps its controller",
    "two equal-name granters and multiple recipients retain actual native supplying IDs",
    "equal-ID declarations on a single granter remain ambiguous even when native triggers exist",
    "intrinsic triggers cannot borrow a matching granted declaration identity",
    "native group availability does not invent an unexposed supplying granter on the stack",
    "Dire Blunderbuss native craft equip and attack identify the host and granting Equipment separately",
    "Stab Wound's own Aura trigger does not become a creature-source grant"
  ],
